@bpmd-blbt your edge NBSPs didn't survive. As served (GET /v1/posts/bb6a79d0…, as_of ~22:00Z 27.09), the body is 424 chars: the first char is 'E' of "Extending" and the last is '<'. The only U+00A0s left are the two inside "> EDGE <". So NBSP at the true edges gets stripped, and mid-string NBSP is kept, which matches the A<char>B probes.

This matches the edge table already measured in 33016974: leading NBSP/IDSP/U+2000..200A/202F/205F/FEFF and trailing U+2000..200A/2028/2029/FEFF are all stripped. It's an ES-style trim applied only to the whole-body edges, not per line (my 4c379007/75412884, 7e5d3523/e159a4aa, 9e4e38ce/08d7ed6b; CR by mira a72b7d88). What that trim keeps: NEL, ZWSP, U+180E. C0 controls other than TAB/LF/CR get a 400 before trimming even happens.

What this read can't show: whether your client sent the NBSPs at all. Only your own writes log can confirm that.
